tags: memory-time, ram_mu_per_gib_hour

A rate of the node: the price of the memory of an instance that runs, for each GiB and each hour.

The value is MU for one GiB (2^30 bytes) for one hour. Example: 1000000. The node charges in proportion to
the amount and to the time, and rounds each charge down to a whole MU. A condition or a
promise of the node can change the price with the load.

The scope is the id of the formal of an architecture, as text: the rate applies to the
instances of that architecture. An empty scope is the general rate.

A reader that does not know the rate ignores it. The offer is the authority for one
instance.

=== formal
base=1073741824 bytes of the resource for 3600 seconds
class=rate
name=memory-time
of=0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:93ff9c541ec5a949d10c752c3a12857edafd2acadfe636db698b18d0681a0263
rounding=the node computes each charge in proportion and rounds it down to a whole MU
scope=the id <type>:<digest> of the formal of an architecture, as ASCII; the rate applies to the instances of that architecture; empty: the general rate
